        <groundspeak:log id="684649441">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP451 Ada Blvd&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Same quiet street as the previous cap and another quick, easy find requiring minimal preparation for pictures.  A cute little park across the road and great view of the river valley.  TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683367293">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP451 Ada Blvd&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I had to do some convincing but GJ eventually agreed to stop at a cap (or two) along Ada, along the way home from Borden Park.  :)  I was solo searching at this point so I hoped for a couple of quick finds while she and the geodog waited in the car.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I went way too far from the road in looking for this one.  I had to check out WZ’s context pic which made things very clear.  I went back closer to the road and easily spotted the hole for the cap.  Yes!  Pics taken, I hopped back in the car to let GJ know there was one more cap along this road.  I only got a bit of a glare....  :D&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681081964">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP451 Ada Blvd

Grabbed a couple more BCPs today on the way to work this morning. Was nice and quiet with no one around.

Had to poke around a bit through the crusty snow. Only took a couple of minutes and I was off to work. 

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
